X: 3
T: Dos Kelbl
N: aka "Donna Donna" or "Dona Dona"
N: The first bar of each bridge phrase held a fraction -- c4/3, g2/3 -- that no
N: partner completed, leaving the bar a fraction short. Those are triplet values
N: in L:1/4, so the source most likely had a quarter triplet there. The four
N: pitches are confirmed by the score at en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dona,_Dona, which
N: this transcription matches note for note in the bars either side; its rhythm
N: is a quarter rest and two eighths. Written here as four plain quarters, the
N: way bar 3 of this transcription squares the same figure off. A reconstruction.
N: Chorus bars 10-11 follow the Wikipedia rhythm (F2, then G3/2 G/), without
N: its English pickup "they", which the Yiddish line has no syllable for.
